diff --git a/beintaskbot-main/docs/crm-relation-sync-contract.md b/beintaskbot-main/docs/crm-relation-sync-contract.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ea5944052aa69e4764de0fa80dced3beff934ec7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/beintaskbot-main/docs/crm-relation-sync-contract.md
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# Inactive relation synchronization contract
+
+`tenant_crm_relation_contract.py` is preparation only. No application route,
+worker, scheduler or migration imports it. It performs no I/O, changes no
+permissions, enables no provider capability and does not remove the existing
+`scoped_relation_sync_not_configured` guard. No real provider calls were used to
+develop or test it.
+
+## Implemented, independent of provider semantics
+
+- An immutable, versioned `RelationIntent` records the exact human actor, source
+  card, source `update` action, changed row, previous and new targets, and the
+  timezone-aware post-change local revision. It represents the existing local
+  deal/contact and contact/company operations, including both source-card
+  directions. It does not authorize them.
+- External identities carry the tenant, provider, provider account and
+  connection generation. Mixed bindings, unrelated source cards, incorrect
+  reverse-card unlink, identity collisions and no-op local changes are rejected.
+  Account and generation values are server-resolved identifiers, never tokens.
+  This is a required data shape, not a new database mapping implementation.
+- Strict serialization accepts only that shape. Full record fields, credentials,
+  provider request bodies, unknown versions and non-update actions are rejected.
+  A canonical content fingerprint distinguishes changed intent under the same
+  event ID. It is not a provider idempotency key or an exactly-once guarantee.
+- An optional `ProviderExpectation` records an adapter contract version and
+  digests of the complete expected and desired remote relation states. It has no
+  default inferred from the local FK. An adapter must include cardinality and
+  relevant metadata such as every Kommo contact and its main-contact flag.
+- A pure observation classifier rejects evidence for a different event,
+  account/generation or adapter contract. Missing observations stay unknown;
+  divergent states are conflicts. An unchanged read after a timeout or an
+  acknowledged request does not prove safe replay. Expired leases are not
+  accepted as proof that a request was never sent.
+
+`expected_observed` and `desired_observed` describe evidence, not permission to
+send or proof this event succeeded. In particular, a desired read-back does not
+prove this event caused the state or resolve an in-flight request. No classifier
+result sends, retries, marks an event synced, or deletes an event.
+
+## Required before connecting this to live operations
+
+1. Approve how the local single-contact FK maps to Kommo's multi-contact lead,
+   including primary selection, replacement and unlink. Confirm BEIN's exact
+   relation-only link/clear and read-back contracts. Validate any idempotency,
+   version or compare-and-set guarantees; headers alone are not proof.
+2. Implement durable account/generation-bound identity storage, including company
+   identities, with explicit handling of old mappings and reconnection. Do not
+   infer a binding from the current connection for a historical mapping.
+3. Atomically persist the local mutation and a separate relation outbox intent.
+   Enforce event-ID/content consistency, serialize changes to the same relation,
+   and check the current local relation and revision before delivery. Do not
+   route a relation event through the existing full-record exporter.
+4. Revalidate the current tenant, active membership and **source card's U
+   permission**, sync policy, mapping bindings and provider connection before
+   delivery, using database fences. A stored actor or successful deserialization
+   is not authorization. Handle revocation, local supersession and changes
+   between checks and provider delivery explicitly.
+5. Define lease ownership, request-outcome evidence, concurrent remote edits,
+   unknown/conflict recovery and read-back consistency for each approved adapter.
+   No automatically retried write can be inferred from the classifier alone.
+6. Verify this complete chain with isolated PostgreSQL and mocked transport,
+   including revocation/concurrency, reconnect, multi-contact preservation,
+   timeout-after-apply and crash recovery, before considering activation.
+
+These are remaining implementation and product prerequisites, not permanent
+product restrictions. The current module supplies a reusable contract without
+choosing the unresolved provider behavior.
+
+## Verification
+
+`python -m pytest -q tests/test_tenant_crm_relation_contract.py` tests synthetic
+round trips, narrow payloads, source-card direction and exact unlink, each binding
+boundary, immutable data, event fingerprints, explicit provider semantics and
+unknown/conflict observations. The existing mocked CRM synchronization workflow
+includes this suite. There is no database schema or enabled dispatcher for it to
+exercise yet; these tests do not establish end-to-end sync readiness.
diff --git a/beintaskbot-main/docs/crm-source-card-relations-ui.md b/beintaskbot-main/docs/crm-source-card-relations-ui.md
